1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:04,200
Have you noticed how changing your life can feel easier when you're somewhere new?

2
00:00:04,291 --> 00:00:10,367
On vacation, you wake up differently. You think differently. Sometimes, you even behave differently.

3
00:00:10,458 --> 00:00:14,633
Then you return home... and somehow, the old version of you returns too.

4
00:00:14,733 --> 00:00:16,667
Here's why that's fascinating.

5
00:00:16,762 --> 00:00:19,100
Your habits aren't stored in willpower alone.

6
00:00:19,209 --> 00:00:21,700
They're strongly connected to your environment.

7
00:00:21,813 --> 00:00:24,867
The same room. The same time. The same cues.

8
00:00:24,958 --> 00:00:32,000
Over time, familiar surroundings can trigger familiar behaviors before you've consciously decided what to do.

9
00:00:32,086 --> 00:00:36,067
Psychologists study something called the habit discontinuity effect.

10
00:00:36,162 --> 00:00:40,100
When your environment changes, old cues can lose some of their power.

11
00:00:40,195 --> 00:00:43,900
And that creates an opportunity to establish new routines.

12
00:00:44,016 --> 00:00:45,667
So here's something to try.

13
00:00:45,767 --> 00:00:48,133
Choose one habit you've struggled to change.

14
00:00:48,243 --> 00:00:52,633
Instead of promising yourself more discipline, change one cue that triggers it.

15
00:00:52,724 --> 00:00:58,000
Move your phone away from your bed. Change where you work. Rearrange your morning routine.

16
00:00:58,103 --> 00:01:03,833
Sometimes, becoming someone new starts with making your old routine harder to repeat.
